  "declaredIdentity": "Tenant+boundaryId, create handler derives from RequestId, draft1=UUIDv5 boundary+draft1, successor draftID supplied from stable request. Create compares initial content even after revisions. Review DecisionId=RequestId but no duplicate/change check; revision/approval retries fail after success. Expected physical append OCC.",
  "invariant": "A boundary has one current draft; approval requires latest accepted review of exact draft revision, an independent/waived actor and strictly increasing approved effective date; exact-scope responsibility changes cannot create retroactive unwaived decision conflict.",
  "boundaryDecision": "narrow",
  "boundaryRationale": "Retain the complete conflict-relevant responsibility/decision state for the current exact boundary draft scope in the same authoritative decision boundary as its review and approval. Do not turn current assignments into independent unconstrained aggregate streams. Narrow accumulated past-scope/version histories and external waiver behavior; a physical draft/publication split is a conditional future design, not the present audit verdict. The collection protects an actual atomic rule over its members: one member cannot hold overlapping work and review/approval responsibilities for the same exact version/revision without an accepted exact waiver, and a later backdated assignment cannot invalidate a prior unwaived review/approval decision. This falls under rule4. Record identity alone does not justify separating assignments.",
